* TO GENERATE THE DELTA-T FIGURE IN THE ONE-HOST SECTION

python3 ./delta_t_evaluator.py  ./fusion_science_use_case.json 1.0 30.0 1.0 --run-sims --num-repeats 5000000  --executable ../build/delta_t_evaluator --sim-executable ../build/redwood_sim_LOWER_BOUND > delta_t_results_LOWER_BOUND.json
python3 ./delta_t_evaluator.py  ./fusion_science_use_case.json 1.0 30.0 1.0 --run-sims --num-repeats 5000000  --executable ../build/delta_t_evaluator --sim-executable ../build/redwood_sim_UPPER_BOUND > delta_t_results_UPPER_BOUND.json

python3 ./delta_t_plotter.py delta_t_results_LOWER_BOUND.json delta_t_results_UPPER_BOUND.json

This needs to be done with two versions of redwood_sim: one there the Dynamic Scheduler uses the upper bound and one where it uses the lower bound. Because the corresponding argument is hardcoded to either true or false in the call to preprocess_host_decisions(), this is a modify/recompile thing.  Would be nice to add this as some argument or as part of the json, but not critical. 

